{
  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_037: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.706) establishes that multimodal with multiprofile, avgpool aggregation, weighted fusion, and a strong image encoder is the dominant design. The remaining untested variable in this top region is the RNA encoder: we've seen pca_n2000 → scvi_n200 yield a modest gain (~1.3%), but scgpt has never been tested. Config_049 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) directly swaps only the RNA encoder in the best-known setup, giving a clean comparison against config_037. This is the highest-value experiment because it (1) exploits the strongest known configuration, (2) tests whether the RNA encoder is still a performance bottleneck or whether scvi_n200 is near-saturated, and (3) if scgpt outperforms, it opens a new optimization axis; if not, it confirms scvi_n200 is sufficient and redirects budget toward other untested dimensions (e.g., transformer aggregation with vit_l). Under a limited budget, this single experiment resolves the most consequential remaining uncertainty about the top-performing region."
}

